


Always use the project logging framework. Do not use System.out.println.

Rebuild with Maven after every code change.

Document any major architectural or module changes.

All PRs must be code reviewed and pass static analysis.

Add clear comments for all public APIs and core methods.

Prefer functional interfaces and lambda expressions.

For core resources, throw business exceptions on null; do not silently handle.

Use unified exception handling; never swallow errors.

Document and communicate all config changes.

Provide basic unit tests for core modules.

Follow layered architecture; avoid cross-module logic.